// Control arm: one agent, one invocation, no coordination to speak of.
// Against Harbor's own single-agent run this prices the OMAR runtime itself;
// against a multi-agent topology it is the baseline the team has to beat.
team Solo[worker : Claude]
{
    input statement : string
    input cwd : string
    output answer : string

    task worker(statement, cwd) -> answer
    "
        The task statement is in the file $(statement). Read it in full first, then
        do the task.
        The task is graded where it lives on this machine, not in your OMAR
        workspace. Make its changes in place, at the paths it names, and use
        $(cwd) as the working directory for anything it leaves relative. Your
        workspace is for your own notes; nothing in it is graded.
        When done, set `answer` to your final response to the task: the text
        it asks you to deliver. If it asks only for changes on disk, one
        paragraph on what you did and how you checked it.
    "
}

main Bench {
    t = Solo()
}
